  "description": "The 2026 election for Texas's 5th Congressional District features incumbent Republican Lance Gooden seeking a fifth term. The district covers parts of Dallas County and extends into rural northeast Texas, including Henderson, Kaufman, Van Zandt, Wood, and Upshur counties. Gooden, a conservative Republican serving on the House Judiciary and Armed Services Committees, faces Democratic nominee Chelsey Hockett, a community advocate from Terrell who defeated Ruth Torres in the May 2026 Democratic primary runoff, and independent candidate Dea Foy. The race tests whether the district, which voted heavily Republican in recent cycles, remains safely in GOP hands during the midterm election.",
